  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Green Cities 2 W2 - Yerevan Bus Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The sovereign loan of up to EUR 20 million to the Republic of Armenia,  which will be co-financed by an investment grant of EUR 5 million from the  Eastern Europe Energy Efficiency and Environment Partnership (&quot;E5P&quot;). The loan  proceeds and investment grant funds will be used to finance the acquisition of  approximately 100 buses of modern 12-metre low-floor Compressed Natural Gas  (&quot;CNG&quot;) buses for the City of Yerevan (the &quot;City&quot;) (the &quot;Project&quot;).  The Project is part of a broader programme aiming to assist the City to reform  its public transport system by financing the renewal of its bus fleet in  anticipation of the restructuring of the bus network.  The Project will improve the reliability, safety and efficiency of public  transport, while CNG technology will reduce air pollution in line with the  Bank&apos;s Green Cities Framework and the Green City Action Plan as approved by the  city of Yerevan in 2017.</narrative>
  </description>
